yxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T16:16:28-07:00","id":1443813,"title":"","content":"in all seriousness,Justin does seem to understand what makes the game work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T18:29:05-07:00","id":1443818,"title":"","content":"I have a really good optimism for this book and the what is coming next. And just a V5 Sabbat that is a complex machination mess full of 50 titles and positions with ten ninja trenchcoat wearing katana and uzi wielders per city working for the Black Hand, that is actually being manipulated by the other truer and deadlier Blacker Hander, is good for me, at least for the first supplement about it. It was, just reading it, a byzantine mess that was as much profound as it was comic booky, and yeah, this has its space in WoD, but by the end of V3 and V20 things were way too out of hand for my own taste. I like Sabbat as a scattered (but scary ass-kicking when united) bunch of fanatic and weird packs, practicing macabre ceremonies, with some esoteric hierarchy that don't get too much in the spotlight. And the way V5 is being more subtle and organized, I think things will get less crazy cook complex. <br /> Who knows, I just like to be positive with my RPGs, cuz the rest is no help","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T19:16:59-07:00","id":1443820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443779-justin-achilli-development-blog-4-13-2021?p=1443792#post1443792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">Also, I love Outstar. She's the best Goth pony.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Outstar is the PerkyGoth.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://di2ponv0v5otw.cloudfront.net/posts/2019/02/02/5c5670a012cd4ab133326780/m_5c5670fcc2e9fe7608bff46d.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443779-justin-achilli-development-blog-4-13-2021?p=1443808#post1443808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some basic observations:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The Sabbat are back</b>: This isn't really too much of a surprise due to the fact they're getting a book but the statement of Sabbat infiltrators implies that they aren't in too bad of a shape and will once more be playing the sects against one another.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Convictions replacing Paths</b>: The statement that especially heinous people have Convictions and that they are justified states to me that they'll be expanding the Conviction system and Touchstones to better reflect Sabbat morality.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Sabbat Attacks Will be a Thing</b>: They won't be the only thing but it seems like the Sword of Caine will be on the offensive again.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Politics with a renewed focus</b>: It seems like some areas will have treaties between the Anarchs and Camarilla that can and will be tested.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>More Romance</b>: I am tickled by this. I probably shouldn't be but I missed when Kindred were married like the Paynes in 1st Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am... underwhelmed. There are no surprises here. We all knew the Sabbat would be back in some form, most of us believed Sabbat paths would be transformed into Convictions (and presumably touchstones) and politics has always been a through line for the game. I am ambivalent about the romance. It is permissible, so long as it remain tragic, ugly, abusive, exploitative, callow, stalkerish, gas-lighting, consumptive, mean spirited, and deadly. These are vampires (and apparently teenagers) we are talking about after all.<br /> <br /> In any case, I'm not seeing any interesting revelations in Achilli's posting, just a confirmation of what we already knew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T20:45:44-07:00","id":1443827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443779-justin-achilli-development-blog-4-13-2021?p=1443820#post1443820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Outstar is the PerkyGoth.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://di2ponv0v5otw.cloudfront.net/posts/2019/02/02/5c5670a012cd4ab133326780/m_5c5670fcc2e9fe7608bff46d.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am... underwhelmed. There are no surprises here. We all knew the Sabbat would be back in some form, most of us believed Sabbat paths would be transformed into Convictions (and presumably touchstones) and politics has always been a through line for the game. I am ambivalent about the romance. It is permissible, so long as it remain tragic, ugly, abusive, exploitative, callow, stalkerish, gas-lighting, consumptive, mean spirited, and deadly. These are vampires (and apparently teenagers) we are talking about after all.<br /> <br /> In any case, I'm not seeing any interesting revelations in Achilli's posting, just a confirmation of what we already knew.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. I see nothing in there that suggests the Sabbat will return to being a true sect with its own cities you can base your campaign in. I don't care about infiltrators. Infiltrators just makes me think that they will be Nephandi with the serial numbers filed off, corrupting the Cammies until they get discovered and become something for the Cammies to punch. Bleech.<br /> <br /> Ah well. I've got Long Road Out of Hell, and it's free. The new &quot;Sabbat&quot; book about infiltrator NPCs who need to be rooted out lest they corrupt the precious darling Cammies and their Bela Swan touchstones is just another book I won't need to waste money on.<br /> <br /> Of course, I could be paranoid and reading way too much into this vagueness, and will listen to reviews when it comes out. But this blog does not make me hopeful. Thank god for Long Road Out of Hell.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T20:50:43-07:00","id":1443828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443779-justin-achilli-development-blog-4-13-2021?p=1443827#post1443827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same. I see nothing in there that suggests the Sabbat will return to being a true sect with its own cities you can base your campaign in. I don't care about infiltrators. Infiltrators just makes me think that they will be Nephandi with the serial numbers filed off, corrupting the Cammies until they get discovered and become something for the Cammies to punch. Bleech.<br /> <br /> Ah well. I've got Long Road Out of Hell, and it's free. The new &quot;Sabbat&quot; book about infiltrator NPCs who need to be rooted out lest they corrupt the precious darling Cammies and their Bela Swan touchstones is just another book I won't need to waste money on.<br /> <br /> Of course, I could be paranoid and reading way too much into this vagueness, and will listen to reviews when it comes out. But this blog does not make me hopeful. Thank god for Long Road Out of Hell.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Given the fact they talk about Sabbat Sieges, it seems that they'll be back to normal. They also talk about Sabbat politics and morality.<br /> <br /> No offense, where did you get the idea it would only be infiltrators?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T08:21:25-07:00","id":1443881,"title":"","content":"This sounds promising. In general, I do think El Bastardo understands Vampire, and he'll get the Sabbat back on track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T14:51:53-07:00","id":1443939,"title":"","content":"Not much new here, so not hopeful at all. But then